uality of sexually transmitted disease case management in rural South Africa.</article-title> <source>Aids</source> <year>1998</year>;<volume>12</volume>:<fpage>2329</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9863876</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11"><label>11</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Connolly</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Influence of HIV-1 coinfection on effective management of abnormal vaginal discharge.</article-title> <source>Sex Transm Dis</source> <year>2003</year>;<volume>30</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12514433</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturm</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Karim</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Impact of Compliance to Antimicrobial Therapy on Microbiological Response of Sexually Transmitted Infections.</article-title> <comment>FIDSSA; 24&#x02013;27 July; Sun City, South Africa</comment>: <year>2005</year></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Connolly</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Male urethritis in South Africa: Impact of HIV co-infection on response to Syndromic Management (Chapter 1 of The Syndromic Management of sexually transmitted diseases: clinical and microbiological response in relation to aetiology, susceptibility patterns and co-infection with HIV-1).</article-title> <publisher-loc>Durban</publisher-loc>: <publisher-name>University of Natal</publisher-name>, <year>2002</year></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturm</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Vanmali</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Association between HIV-1 infection, the etiology of genital ulcer disease, and response to syndromic management.</article-title> <source>Sex Transm Dis</source> <year>2003</year>;<volume>30</volume>:<fpage>241</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12616144</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O&#x02019;Farrell</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoosen</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kharsany</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Sexually transmitted pathogens in pregnant women in a rural South African community.</article-title> <source>Genitourin Med</source> <year>1989</year>;<volume>65</volume>:<fpage>276</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2807289</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Colvin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Abdool Karim</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Connolly</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>HIV infection and asymptomatic sexually transmitted infections in a rural South African community.</article-title> <source>Int J STD AIDS</source> <year>1998</year>;<volume>9</volume>:<fpage>548</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9764941</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sturm</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Ndovela</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Pregnant women as a reservoir of undetected sexually transmitted diseases in rural South Africa: implications for disease control.</article-title> <source>Am J Public Health</source> <year>1998</year>;<volume>88</volume>:<fpage>1243</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9702160</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Myer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Abdool Karim</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lombard</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Treatment of maternal syphilis in rural South Africa: effect of multiple doses of benzathine penicillin on pregnancy loss.</article-title> <source>Trop Med Int Health</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>9</volume>:<fpage>1216</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15548319</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Ndovela</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Family planning services in developing countries: an opportunity to treat asymptomatic and unrecognised genital tract infections?</article-title> <source>Genitourin Med</source> <year>1997</year>;<volume>73</volume>:<fpage>558</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9582484</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sturm</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturm</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Trends in the prevalence of sexually transmitted infections and HIV in pregnant women in KwazuluNatal from 1995 till 2002.</article-title> <comment>South African AIDS conference; Durban</comment>: <year>2003</year></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sturm</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Connolly</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Khan</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Vaginal tampons as specimen collection device for the molecular diagnosis of non-ulcerative sexually transmitted infections in antenatal clinic attendees.</article-title> <source>Int J STD AIDS</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>15</volume>:<fpage>94</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15006070</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Department of Health</collab> <article-title>National HIV and syphilis antenatal sero-prevalence survey in South Africa 2004</article-title>; <year>2004</year></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b23"><label>23</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spiegelhalter</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Winbugs User Manual (Version 1.4.1). Version 1.4.1 ed.</article-title> <publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc>: <publisher-name>Imperial College and Medical Research Council</publisher-name>, <year>2003</year></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b24"><label>24</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>IMC</given-names></name><name><surname>Pillay</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Molecular epidemiology of recently emergent ciprofloxacin-resistant <italic>Neisseria gonorrhoeae</italic> in South Africa.</article-title> <source>Sex Transm Dis</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>33</volume>:<fpage>357</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16572037</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b25"><label>25</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Plenary on Drug Resistance in <italic>Neisseria gonorrhoeae</italic> in South Africa.</article-title> <comment>FIDSSA 2nd Joint Congress; 28&#x02013;31 October 2007; Cape Town, South Africa</comment>: <year>2007</year></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b26"><label>26</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grosskurth</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Mwijarubi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Todd</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Operational performance of an STD control programme in Mwanza Region, Tanzania.</article-title> <source>Sex Trans Inf</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>76</volume>:<fpage>426</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>36</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b27"><label>27</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moodley</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturm</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Management of vaginal discharge syndrome: how effective is our strategy?</article-title> <source>Int J Antimicrob Agents</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>24</volume><issue>(Suppl 1)</issue>:<fpage>S4</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15364298</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b28"><label>28</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Abdool Karim</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Unrecognized sexually transmitted infections in rural South African women: a hidden epidemic.</article-title> <source>Bull WHO</source> <year>1999</year>;<volume>77</volume>:<fpage>22</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10063657</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b29"><label>29</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buve</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Changalucha</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayaud</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>How many patients with a sexually transmitted infection are cured by health services? A study from Mwanza region, Tanzania.</article-title> <source>Trop Med Int Health</source> <year>2001</year>;<volume>6</volume>:<fpage>971</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11737832</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>